       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day. That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg/day for adults, and an overdose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals**, which totals 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **A lower dose**, such as 500 mg BID or 1,000 mg BID. Immediate-release metformin is usually started low and titrated up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 2550 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly."
