       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose. No indication I know of supports it, and it carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis. This is true even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose you can titrate up.\n- **Check for a unit or transcription mix-up.** 2,550 mg is the daily maximum, so it may have been entered as the per-dose amount by mistake.\n- **Use your institution's pathway for exceptional dosing.** If you have a reason for going above the maximum, a pharmacy consult or a formal override process would be the right route. I shouldn't bypass that check.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
